{#
    One product in a listing.

    Overridable per listing element (conshoTileTemplate) rather than per
    product: the same article appears as a tile, on a detail page and in a
    basket, so a template chosen at the record could serve only one of them.

    Title and teaser come input encoded from the database. Templates in the
    @Contao namespace are escaped with Contao's own strategy, which does not
    encode "&amp;" a second time — the filter element relies on the same.

    Variables: product (ProductTile), imageSize, showsNet, garan (nested GARAN
    label or null, GA8).

    showsNet is a statement about the VISITOR, not about the article, which is
    why it is passed in rather than read off the tile: whether a price carries
    the tax is the same answer for every tile on the page (C-4).
#}
{% use "@Contao/component/_figure.html.twig" %}

<article class="consho-tile" data-product="{{ product.id }}">
    {# figure() and Contao's figure component, not an <img> built by hand —
       contao_figure() is deprecated since 5.0. Consho brings no image handling
       of its own; the size comes from the element. A deleted file yields no
       figure and no empty frame. #}
    {% set figure = product.image ? figure(product.image, imageSize) : null %}
    {% if figure %}
        {{ block("figure_component") }}
    {% endif %}

    {# Without a product page in the shop the url is empty — the tile then
       stays a tile rather than linking nowhere. #}
    <h3 class="consho-tile__title">
        {%- if product.url -%}
            <a href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title }}</a>
        {%- else -%}
            {{ product.title }}
        {%- endif -%}
    </h3>

    {% if product.teaser %}
        <p class="consho-tile__teaser">{{ product.teaser }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    {#- GA8: the nested GARAN label, only where the operator set one; the
        full label stays on the product page (GA3). -#}
    {% if garan|default(null) %}
        {% include "@Contao/consho/garan_nested.html.twig" with {garan: garan} only %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if product.formattedPrice %}
        {#- Block H (H-2): a promotion below the lowest price of the 30 days
            before it began — the badge, and that price struck through. Only
            then: a promotion that is not below it reduces nothing (B). -#}
        {% if product.formattedCompare|default('') %}
            <p class="consho-tile__badge consho-tile__badge--promotion">{{ "CONSHO.promotion.badge"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        <p class="consho-tile__price">
            {#- "ab" only when the variants genuinely differ in price. Writing it
                where they do not suggests a cheaper one exists. -#}
            {% if product.isFrom %}{{ "CONSHO.priceFrom"|trans({}, "contao_default") }} {% endif %}
            {#- Rounded and formatted in the page's language (MoneyFormatter).
                product.price holds the raw decimal for templates of their own. -#}
            {{ product.formattedPrice }}
        </p>
        {% if product.formattedCompare|default('') %}
            <p class="consho-tile__reference"><del>{{ product.formattedCompare }}</del> {{ "CONSHO.promotion.reference"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        {# Which of the two sentences appears is decided in the controller and
           travels on showsNet — the template never asks who is logged in. #}
        {% if not untaxed|default(false) or (shipped ?? true) %}<p class="consho-tile__tax">{{ untaxed|default(false) ? "CONSHO.priceShippingOnly"|trans({}, "contao_default") : ("CONSHO." ~ ((shipped ?? true) ? "priceTaxNotice" : "priceTaxOnly") ~ (showsNet|default(false) ? "Net" : ""))|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</p>{% endif %}
        {#- Abo-2b, P89: the figure is the one-time price, and the product can
            also be had as a plan — which one and for how much, the product
            page says. After the tax notice, which belongs to the price
            (Abo-2b). -#}
        {#- Block G (G7): only where stock is kept, never the number. #}
        {% if product.stock|default('') %}
            <p class="consho-tile__stock consho-tile__stock--{{ product.stock }}">{{ ("CONSHO.stock." ~ product.stock)|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</p>
        {% endif %}
        {% if product.alsoSubscription|default(false) %}
            <p class="consho-tile__subscription">{{ "CONSHO.tile.alsoSubscription"|trans({}, "contao_default") }}</p>
        {% endif %}

        {#
            Purchase button on the tile, switched on at the list element.
            Three conditions, and all three must hold:

            - `tilePurchase` — the operator wanted it on this list. Off by
              default, so that an overview does not turn into a shop shelf
              unasked.
            - `product.isBuyable` — no main product WITH variants. There is no
              buyable article there until someone has chosen; the tile then
              links to the detail page as before.
            - `product.formattedPrice` — without a price there is no offer, and
              a purchase button above an empty price line would be one.

            ⚠️ Quantity WITHOUT a field: the product's minimum quantity, silently.
            Whoever wants another goes to the detail page or changes it in the
            cart. A number field per tile would make every tile taller and bring
            the step size along, which nobody sees there.

            ⚠️ NO CSRF field, unlike the cart and the checkout: the add route is
            exempt (`_token_check: false`, C11) and protected by `SameSite=Lax`
            plus an Origin check. That is exactly why — a list is cached shared,
            and a token in it would be some other visitor's.
        #}
        {% if tilePurchase|default(false) and product.isBuyable and product.formattedPrice and product.stock|default('') != 'unavailable' %}
            <form class="consho-tile__purchase" method="post" action="{{ path("consho_cart_add") }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="article" value="{{ product.id }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="page" value="{{ purchasePage|default(0) }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="{{ product.purchaseQuantity }}">
                <button type="submit" class="consho-tile__purchase-submit">
                    {#- The title belongs in the label: on a page with twelve
                        tiles a screen reader would otherwise read "In den Warenkorb"
                        twelve times without a difference. -#}
                    {{ "CONSHO.tile.purchase"|trans([product.title], "contao_default") }}
                </button>
            </form>
        {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
</article>
